  "summary": "Overnight markets stayed defensive: the S&P 500 closed at 7416.59, gold held near 3853, and Treasuries found a modest bid while short-end yields remain elevated after a multi-day backup of roughly 26\u201332 basis points. WTI settled at 85.72 and Brent at 92.44, in line with crude slipping toward $85 as Middle East exports recover even as Hormuz tensions intensified with a tanker strike and a third U.S. carrier in the region. The dollar firmed against G10; USD/JPY sat at 159.60 near a five-year extreme and USDCAD pressed a five-year high. Euro-area resilience and firm U.S. activity keep ECB hike pricing in focus, while Chair Warsh\u2019s warnings on AI disappointment added to risk sentiment. Watch Australia wages and labour force, euro-area HICP, Japan CPI, Canada retail trade, U.S. retail sales already in the tape, later PCE, income and GDP, plus Bank of Canada, RBNZ, and the FOMC.",
